R('b3-q20','b','copy,merge','COPY INTO idempotency; Apply source changes with MERGE',
 'COPY INTO normally skips files already recognized as ingested, so overwriting the same filename is not a reliable update propagation design. Deliver corrections as new input and apply business-key updates to the Delta target.',
 'File ingestion idempotency does not automatically implement row-level correction semantics.',
 'Reloading every file can duplicate records and wastes work unless a carefully designed full-rebuild strategy is used. It is not the incremental correction approach requested.',
 'New correction files can be discovered and then merged by the relevant record keys. This separates reliable new-file discovery from applying updates to existing rows.',
 'Recreating the target discards its normal continuity and repeats all ingestion. It is unnecessary for individual corrected records and can disrupt consumers.',
 'Overwriting the whole target on every run is a full replacement strategy, not incremental correction handling. It adds work and risks losing records if the replacement input is incomplete.')
R('b3-q21','a','salesforce,lakeflow-connect','Salesforce ingestion connector; Feature availability',
 'The managed Salesforce connector supports incremental ingestion into Unity Catalog-governed tables with a managed authoring/orchestration experience. Check its documented supported objects, authentication methods, and schema-evolution limitations.',
 'JSON describes the source data shape; it does not mean file ingestion is required when a managed application connector exists.',
 'A names the built-in managed Salesforce ingestion path and governed Delta target. This directly fits low-code managed ingestion from the application.',
 'A custom REST notebook can be built but requires maintaining pagination, credentials, retries, and incremental state. That does not meet the minimal custom-management requirement as directly.',
 'Auto Loader reads exported files after another process creates them. It is not the direct managed Salesforce connector requested.',
 'A DBFS file-arrival idea neither connects to Salesforce nor establishes supported managed source ingestion. File-arrival triggers and application connectors are different components.')
R('b3-q22','b','convert-managed','Streaming behavior; Restart streams after conversion',
 'External-to-managed conversion changes the underlying managed location and requires restarting existing streams with the same configuration. Preserve checkpoint state so the stream can continue using the supported redirect behavior.',
 'A required restart is not a reason to discard exactly-once progress.',
 'Additional storage permissions are not the documented generic remedy for the conversion-related stopped stream. Investigate a real authorization error separately rather than assume one here.',
 'B follows the conversion reference: restart the stream using its existing settings so it picks up the converted table/redirect. This preserves its recovery state.',
 'REFRESH TABLE refreshes relation/cache metadata but does not rewrite or restart the streaming query’s checkpoint execution. It is not the documented stream recovery step.',
 'Deleting the checkpoint starts a new stream history and can cause reprocessing. The conversion guidance says to restart with the same configuration, not erase progress.')
R('b3-q23',None,'auto-schema,delta','Schema evolution modes; Delta schema evolution',
 'A supported add-columns configuration can eventually add a nullable userAgent field, but Auto Loader’s addNewColumns mode first updates schema metadata and fails the running query until restart. Delta sink evolution must also be configured; no option describes the full stated execution behavior.',
 'Separate source-schema discovery, stream restart, and target-table schema evolution.',
 'New nullable columns do not require backfilling all old data to a non-null default. Older records typically read as NULL for the newly added field.',
 'B describes a common eventual result after source restart and compatible Delta sink schema evolution. Those settings and the intermediate failure/restart are omitted, so the blanket behavior is not fully established.',
 'The source stream can fail under addNewColumns, but the schema is updated automatically before restart rather than universally requiring a manual ALTER TABLE. This description is incomplete too.',
 'Silently ignoring every new field is associated with other configured modes, not generic schema evolution enabled. It contradicts the intended add-column behavior.',status='source-and-sink-evolution-unspecified')
R('b3-q24',None,'kafka,lakeflow-connect','Kafka streaming source; Connector types',
 'Kafka has a documented Structured Streaming ingestion path, but the retrieved managed-connector references do not establish the specific Snowflake incremental connector assumed by B. A strict sub-30-second end-to-end latency also requires measured processing/queueing bounds.',
 'Verify each named connector and its change-tracking semantics; do not infer them from a generic connector family.',
 'A full refresh rereads unchanged customer data and violates the incremental requirement. A Kafka stream alone does not fix that second source behavior.',
 'B is the intended architecture only if the named Snowflake managed incremental connector and its actual change semantics are available. That specific prerequisite was not verified from the accessible official pages.',
 'The Python interface is spark.readStream without calling it as shown, and an hourly time filter is not the specified four-hour governed change-capture plan. Timestamp polling also needs a reliable change watermark and delete strategy.',
 'Polling all rows and merging may avoid duplicate target keys but still rereads unchanged source data. It does not meet the stated prevent-reprocessing requirement.',status='named-connector-unverified')
R('b3-q25',None,'lakeflow-connect,salesforce','Managed connector concepts; Connector-specific feature availability',
 'A managed connector is the desired operational model, but the SaaS application is unnamed and CDC, deletes, OAuth modes, and schema evolution vary by connector. A cannot be certified as a universal all-SaaS capability without the actual supported connector.',
 'A connector family does not guarantee every source supports every change, authentication, or schema operation.',
 'A describes the desired managed feature set and is the likely design intent if that source connector supports all of it. The official feature matrices are source-specific, so the unspecified application prevents full verification.',
 'Custom API/CDC/OAuth logic in pipelines shifts maintenance back to the team. Auto Loader only manages exported files rather than the SaaS extraction itself.',
 'Direct custom API batches require implementing change handling, retries, and schema logic. That does not satisfy the stated fully managed low-maintenance requirement.',
 'A standard/custom connector plus hand-built MERGE and monitoring is more manual than the requested managed service. It does not establish native support for all required source changes.',status='source-specific-capabilities-unspecified')
R('b3-q26','a','file-events,auto-loader','File notification mode; Existing files',
 'File notifications/file events scale ongoing discovery without repeatedly listing the full directory. Existing files can still be included during initialization; events are not a claim that historical files never need an initial discovery pass.',
 'Notification mode does not exclude historical files, and exactly-once state is retained through supported discovery-mode changes.',
 'A selects the recommended scalable ongoing notification design while allowing the initial existing-file backlog. Account for initial discovery and supported includeExistingFiles/checkpoint behavior.',
 'Directory listing is not generally documented as faster for a large ongoing workload, and legacy incremental listing has ordering assumptions. The asserted universal performance advantage is unsupported.',
 'Switching discovery modes is supported with retained progress, so this can be engineered, but it adds an unnecessary manual phase. It is not required just because historical files exist.',
 'Notifications mode can handle pre-existing data through initial discovery. It is not restricted to use only after some separate process empties the historical backlog.')
R('b3-q27','c','salesforce,sqlserver,auto-loader,lakeflow-connect','Connector feature availability; SQL Server change tracking; Auto Loader',
 'Choose supported managed application/database ingestion for Salesforce and SQL Server, and file ingestion for ADLS. Unity Catalog governs outputs; source gateways/networking and connector-specific schema limits still need setup.',
 'File ingestion is not an API extractor, and managed database CDC has source prerequisites.',
 'A partner service may be viable, but the unsupported most-comprehensive claim does not establish a necessary solution. Native supported connectors already address the named source categories.',
 'Assuming one uniform managed connector behavior for all three source types skips source-specific support and setup. ADLS JSON files have a directly documented Auto Loader path.',
 'C uses the appropriate native source mechanisms and governed downstream pipelines. SQL Server CDC/change tracking and network/gateway requirements remain necessary, and not every schema change is automatically supported.',
 'Auto Loader cannot extract Salesforce APIs or SQL Server CDC by itself. Adding custom extraction abandons the goal of minimizing source-specific engineering effort.')
R('b3-q28','d','auto-loader,auto-schema','cloudFiles source; Schema inference configuration',
 'Select cloudFiles as the streaming source and set cloudFiles.format to json. Schema and checkpoint locations are managed by pipelines or need appropriate configuration when the stream is executed standalone.',
 'The source provider and the incoming encoding are separate settings.',
 'Using format json selects the ordinary file source rather than Auto Loader. Setting a cloudFiles option does not change that provider.',
 'B chooses cloudFiles but omits the required incoming cloudFiles.format value. The source cannot assume JSON from the generic input path.',
 'The option key format is not the documented cloudFiles.format setting. It does not correctly declare the Auto Loader file encoding.',
 'D uses readStream.format("cloudFiles") and option("cloudFiles.format", "json"). That is the supported Auto Loader source pattern among the choices.',
 'E does not select the cloudFiles provider. Supplying only one cloudFiles option does not turn the default reader format into Auto Loader.')
R('b3-q29','c','merge','WHEN NOT MATCHED BY SOURCE',
 'WHEN NOT MATCHED BY SOURCE applies to target rows with no corresponding source match. Its DELETE action can remove those target-only rows atomically within the MERGE transaction.',
 'NOT MATCHED normally refers to source-only insert candidates; BY SOURCE changes the focus to unmatched target rows.',
 'WHEN MATCHED BY SOURCE is not the supported clause here and setting columns NULL is not deleting rows. It cannot implement the requested target-only deletion.',
 'MATCHED AND needs a valid condition and concerns rows that match both sides. It is not the target-unmatched-by-source branch.',
 'C uses the exact supported branch for target rows absent from the source. Add an appropriate limiting condition when only a bounded target region should be synchronized.',
 'WHEN NOT MATCHED is the source-without-target branch and does not support deleting a target row that does not exist in that branch. It targets the wrong unmatched side.')
R('b3-q30','a','kafka,ldp-python','Read from Kafka; Pipeline dataset definitions',
 'The legacy pipeline function must return a Kafka readStream DataFrame configured with brokers and topic subscription. SDP naming changes do not make Kafka a cloudFiles file path.',
 'Check the source provider before parsing Kafka value payloads downstream.',
 'A configures format kafka, bootstrap servers, subscribe, starting offsets, and load inside the dataset function. It is the supported legacy ingestion pattern shown.',
 'B uses cloudFiles against a Kafka broker URI. Auto Loader discovers object-store files and does not replace the Kafka connector.',
 'C treats a broker/topic string as a SQL relation without a configured Kafka connector. The source syntax does not establish Kafka ingestion.',
 'D likewise uses cloud_files for a Kafka URI and projects value fields without decoding a Kafka source. It confuses cloud-file ingestion with message-bus ingestion.')
reuse('b3-q31','b1-q40','acde',None)
R('b3-q32','a','streaming','AvailableNow: Incremental batch processing',
 'AvailableNow processes data available at the start of the run across as many micro-batches as needed. Deprecated Once processes a single batch and does not express the same bounded multi-batch guarantee.',
 'As many batches as required is the key distinction between AvailableNow and Once.',
 'A uses trigger(availableNow=True), the documented incremental catch-up trigger. Rate limits can split the available backlog into multiple micro-batches.',
 'processingTime expects a supported interval rather than once. It schedules repeated processing rather than selecting this bounded catch-up mode.',
 'continuous="once" is not the supported bounded trigger and continuous processing is not the intended Databricks mode here. It does not implement the requested multi-batch catch-up.',
 'once=True is the older single-batch trigger and is deprecated for these workloads. It is not equivalent to processing all backlog across as many batches as required.')
